{
  "$comment": [
    "Audit spec §6.6: the exact JSON of each answer of the audit routes and of the audit service (audit.list, audit.export, audit.verify), and every audit error body. Names are paths: list.entries, verify.broken.seq_gap, error.audit_query_invalid.to/order (a \"/\" suffix names the second rule of a parameter; `repeated` is any parameter given twice).",
    "list.* are what audit.list resolves (the body of GET /api/audit); verify.* what audit.verify resolves (GET /api/audit/verify, or goblin-admin verify-audit --json: those with `journal` and `foreignLines`, and verify.incomplete.no_key and verify.incomplete.unknown_key, come only from the CLI); export.* are the answers of GET /api/audit/export, with `body` as text (a CSV starts with the BOM, \\ufeff) and the {rows, more, filename, contentType} audit.export resolves beside it; error.* are {status, headers, body}.",
    "Volatile values are written as \"<seq>\" (an entry number: seq, ref, a cursor), \"<ms>\" (a time or a duration in milliseconds), \"<hash>\" (64 hex digits), \"<id>\" (a session, request, delivery, instance or key id, or a build), \"<time>\" (a time as auditTime() writes it inside a text), \"<iso>\" (an ISO 8601 time in a CSV cell) and \"<stamp>\" (the YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS of an export file name). Numbers inside texts are written with thousands separators when real.",
    "verify.anchors holds every anchor that can stand in an intact log; the head-mismatch audit.gap is in verify.broken.log_truncated (it is always log_truncated) and the key.reset that names a head in verify.incomplete.key_reset (the rows it covers are unverifiable).",
    "Phase 0 contract (frozen): changed only through the integrator, with the agreement of every lane that uses it. Changed at integration: verify.incomplete.unknown_key added (journal lines under a key the keyring does not hold, which no reset removed, leave the result incomplete; the CLI only)."
  ],
